1
00:10:22,105 --> 00:10:28,105
On the Beach is a drama, science fiction, tv movie
film directed by Russell Mulcahy.

2
00:20:44,210 --> 00:20:50,210
The world has finally managed to blow itself up and only Australia has been spared from
nuclear destruction and a gigantic wave of radiation is floating in on the breezes.

3
00:31:06,315 --> 00:31:12,315
One American sub located in the Pacific has survived and
is met with disdain by the Australians.

4
00:41:28,421 --> 00:41:34,421
The calculations of Australia's most renowned
scientist says the country is doomed.

5
00:51:50,526 --> 00:51:56,526
However, one of his rivals says that he is wrong.

6
01:02:12,631 --> 01:02:18,631
He believes that a 1000 people can be relocated to the northern hemisphere,
where his assumptions indicate the radiation levels may be lower.

7
01:12:34,736 --> 01:12:40,736
The American Captain is asked to take a mission to the
north to determine which scientist is right.

8
01:22:56,842 --> 01:23:02,842
Cmdr. Dwight Towers, played by Armand Assante.

9
01:33:18,947 --> 01:33:24,947
Moira Davidson, played by Rachel Ward.

10
01:43:41,052 --> 01:43:47,052
Dr. Julian Osborne, played by Bryan Brown.

11
01:54:03,157 --> 01:54:09,157
Mary Davidson Holmes, played by Jacqueline McKenzie.

12
02:04:25,263 --> 02:04:31,263
Lt. Peter Holmes, played by Grant Bowler.

13
02:14:47,368 --> 02:14:53,368
Jenny Holmes, played by Tieghan Webber.

14
02:25:09,473 --> 02:25:15,473
On the Beach is a 2000 apocalyptic drama television film directed by Russell
Mulcahy and starring Armand Assante, Bryan Brown, and Rachel Ward.

15
02:35:31,578 --> 02:35:37,578
In America, it aired on Showtime on 28 May 2000 and
in Australia it aired on Channel 7.

16
02:45:53,684 --> 02:45:59,684
The film is a remake of a 1959 film, which was also based on the 1957 novel by Nevil Shute, but updates the setting of the story to the
film's then-future of 2006, starting with placing the crew on a fictional Los Angeles-class submarine, USS Charleston (SSN-704).

17
02:56:15,789 --> 02:56:21,789
The film explores themes of australia, based on novel or
book, submarine, atomic bomb, dystopia.

18
03:06:37,894 --> 03:06:43,894
The tone is emotional and thought_provoking.
